                            <comment id="493917" author="adilger" created="Fri, 1 May 2026 05:55:10 +0000">&lt;p&gt;This functionality is very similar to &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20211" title="FLR-ECRO: allow &amp;#39;truncate(file, 0)&amp;#39; and &amp;#39;open(file, O_TRUNC)&amp;#39; on degraded EC file" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20211"&gt;LU-20211&lt;/a&gt;, which is also proposing to "delete" a file that is contains inaccessible OST objects when it is truncated to zero, .  That would push any inaccessible objects over to trash (or delete them) instead of failing an "overwrite" of the file.  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
